   "body": "## Summary\n\n`muse.py` opens the gateway WebSocket without TLS certificate verification, and the Noise XX handshake does not authenticate the server's static key. Together this leaves the gateway session (the `hatch_token` in the URL query and all traffic inside the Noise channel) open to an on-path attacker. Because this runs as an MCP server, tampered responses would also flow into the calling agent's context.\n\n## Details\n\n`muse.py`, in the gateway class `__init__` (line 189 at `965cc2f`):\n\n```python\nself.ws = WebSocket()\nself.ws.connect(url, impersonate=\"chrome\", timeout=20)\n```\n\nWith curl_cffi 0.16.3, `WebSocket.connect` passes `verify_list=[None, verify]`, and `requests/utils.py` computes `disable_verify = verify is False or not base_verify and verify is None`. When neither the session nor the call sets `verify`, this evaluates to `True`, so `CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER` / `CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST` end up as 0. The HTTPS calls made with `curl_cffi.requests` (`/api/auth/check`, `/api/hatch/token`, `/api/session`) do verify certificates, so the `hatch_sess` cookie itself is not affected.\n\nThe Noise handshake uses a fresh random static key and never checks the responder's static public key after `read_message`, so it does not compensate for the missing TLS check.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nUsing the same call pattern as `muse.py`:\n\n```python\nfrom curl_cffi.requests import WebSocket\nWebSocket().connect(\"wss://self-signed.badssl.com/\", impersonate=\"chrome\", timeout=15)\n# TLS handshake succeeds; fails later only at the WebSocket upgrade (curl 22)\n\nWebSocket().connect(\"wss://self-signed.badssl.com/\", impersonate=\"chrome\", timeout=15, verify=True)\n# curl: (60) SSL certificate OpenSSL verify result: self signed certificate\n```\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n```diff\n-        self.ws.connect(url, impersonate=\"chrome\", timeout=20)\n+        self.ws.connect(url, impersonate=\"chrome\", timeout=20, verify=True)\n```\n\nWith this change applied locally, `muse-mcp doctor` still connects normally to `hatch.metaaivm.com`, and the self-signed endpoint above is rejected.\n\nEnvironment: muse-mcp `965cc2f`, curl_cffi 0.16.3, mcp 1.30.0, Python 3.12, macOS.\n\nThe same issue exists upstream in muse-cli: https://github.com/nikships/muse-cli/issues/1\n",
